          "source": "",
          "thread": "Bybit signing exploit accountability",
          "why": "Aggregating over 300 clicks across multiple articles, the revelation that Safe's proxy logic could be rewritten via DELEGATECALL after hardware wallet verification was skipped forced readers to confront how institutional-grade infrastructure becomes an attack surface."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://safe.global",
          "thread": "Safe as integrated DeFi product layer",
          "why": "The single top-clicked story — native swaps via CoW Swap — signals readers see Safe evolving from a security primitive into a full DeFi app layer with swaps, portfolio dashboards, and batch transactions."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "DAO treasury control and drama",
          "why": "The 0xPauly story drew 266 clicks because it crystallizes a core tension: multisig wallets are trustless by design, but who holds the keys to a community treasury is an inherently political question with no on-chain enforcement."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "$SAFE token governance and speculation",
          "why": "Speculation around token transferability and a $3B+ FDV launch attracted readers tracking how infrastructure protocols monetize via governance tokens and what DAO control actually means in practice."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://safe.global",
          "thread": "Cross-chain expansion and real-world payments",
          "why": "Safenet and the Monerium Euro payments partnership collectively drew readers watching Safe move beyond Ethereum mainnet security into cross-chain asset management and fiat settlement infrastructure."
        },
        {
          "source": "https://safefoundation.org/blog/history-of-safe",
          "thread": "Institutional adoption as legitimacy signal",
          "why": "The Ethereum Foundation setting up a 3-of-5 Safe multisig and Safe securing one-third of EVM DeFi TVL confirmed to readers that Safe is the de facto standard for on-chain institutional treasury management."
        }
      ]
